WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:09.818
Welcome to Preshift Rota, from Williams, Stanley and Co. and Preshift.

2
00:00:09.818 --> 00:00:12.720
The rota is where culture and cost meet.

3
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.798
Get it wrong and the team is run ragged on a busy night, or padded out

4
00:00:17.798 --> 00:00:20.917
on a quiet one, and the numbers never hold.

5
00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:27.569
Preshift sizes each shift to the forecast, shares the hard shifts fairly, protects rest, gets the

6
00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:31.661
rota out in good time, and gives people a say in when they work.

7
00:00:31.661 --> 00:00:36.201
And it costs every shift the way payroll will, so labour in the P and L

8
00:00:36.201 --> 00:00:38.503
is true before payroll has even run.

9
00:00:38.953 --> 00:00:40.776
This is the public demo.

10
00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:44.574
Anyone can start a private copy of a sample group:

11
00:00:44.574 --> 00:00:49.664
two companies, three London sites, real teams, rates and forecasts.

12
00:00:49.664 --> 00:00:54.374
Nobody else sees what you change, and it is wiped at midnight.

13
00:00:54.374 --> 00:00:55.969
Press Start the demo.

14
00:00:56.432 --> 00:01:01.381
Each Monday, What's new offers that week's changes as a short walkthrough.

15
00:01:01.381 --> 00:01:07.132
One card per change, each opening the screen it changed, and only for the sections you

16
00:01:07.132 --> 00:01:07.400
use.

17
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.272
Let's look at the first few.

18
00:01:09.723 --> 00:01:15.034
Next takes you to the following change, on its own screen, with the right site and

19
00:01:15.034 --> 00:01:16.200
view already open.

20
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:21.123
Two minutes, and nobody has to read a release note to find out what changed.

21
00:01:21.574 --> 00:01:25.536
You can replay it any time from What's new, top right.

22
00:01:25.536 --> 00:01:28.030
Let's close it and start the tour.

23
00:01:32.486 --> 00:01:38.911
Everything sits in one bar across the top, grouped the way a general manager runs the

24
00:01:38.911 --> 00:01:39.289
week.

25
00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:39.894
Plan it.

26
00:01:39.894 --> 00:01:41.557
Run the hours and pay.

27
00:01:41.557 --> 00:01:43.069
Look after the team.

28
00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:46.622
Then the money, and the organisation behind it.

29
00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:51.043
Open a group and each section says, in a line, what it is for.

30
00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:56.678
People see only the sections their roles allow, and an owner can switch off features the

31
00:01:56.678 --> 00:02:01.737
business does not use, so a GM is not wading through forty sections to use ten.

32
00:02:02.187 --> 00:02:05.192
Go to a section finds any screen by name.

33
00:02:05.192 --> 00:02:10.395
Press the slash key from anywhere, type a few letters, and press enter.

34
00:02:10.845 --> 00:02:16.016
Your own menu, top right, holds your profile and, in the demo, Viewing as:

35
00:02:16.016 --> 00:02:22.095
see the product as any of thirteen people, a general manager, a supervisor, a chef, the

36
00:02:22.095 --> 00:02:23.283
finance director.

37
00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:29.013
Each sees exactly what their roles permit, and the server enforces the same rules.

38
00:02:29.463 --> 00:02:34.796
Under the heading sits the week picker, with a badge telling you whether the week is

39
00:02:34.796 --> 00:02:36.192
published to the team.

40
00:02:36.192 --> 00:02:42.922
And along the bottom, Tell Preshift takes plain English instructions, while Shifty, in the corner, answers

41
00:02:42.922 --> 00:02:43.556
questions.

42
00:02:43.556 --> 00:02:45.207
We will come back to both.

43
00:02:49.383 --> 00:02:52.451
Under every heading runs one line of numbers:

44
00:02:52.451 --> 00:02:58.722
labour as a percentage of sales against target, sales, labour, how far inside the budget you

45
00:02:58.722 --> 00:03:00.086
are, and compliance.

46
00:03:00.086 --> 00:03:02.199
Here it is for the whole group.

47
00:03:02.651 --> 00:03:05.752
Full P and L opens the statement behind it.

48
00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:12.675
Forecast sales, then wages, holiday accrual, employer N I and pension, the labour cost that ties

49
00:03:12.675 --> 00:03:17.867
to the journal, contribution after labour, and every day against target.

50
00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:21.972
Below, every site side by side, grouped by company.

51
00:03:21.972 --> 00:03:29.850
Forecast sales, loaded labour, labour percentage against each site's own target, the variance in pounds, sales

52
00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:33.933
per labour hour, paid hours, and whether the rota is out.

53
00:03:33.933 --> 00:03:36.583
A site with a blocking issue says so.

54
00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:37.899
Further down:

55
00:03:37.899 --> 00:03:44.025
rest overrides published in the last four weeks, cross site cover, and travel between sites.

56
00:03:44.025 --> 00:03:49.087
Journey times come from the T f L planner, so the rota blocks a move between

57
00:03:49.087 --> 00:03:51.817
two sites that nobody could make in time.

58
00:03:52.268 --> 00:03:56.175
And one press of Build from forecast builds every site in scope:

59
00:03:56.175 --> 00:04:01.120
each site with its own team first, then cover from people who have agreed to work

60
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.036
at other sites.

61
00:04:06.197 --> 00:04:08.770
Open a site, and you land on its rota.

62
00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.056
This is Marylebone.

63
00:04:10.056 --> 00:04:15.134
The same line of numbers sits under the heading, so the cost of the week is

64
00:04:15.134 --> 00:04:17.165
never more than a glance away.

65
00:04:17.615 --> 00:04:22.737
Coming up flags what the week needs your view on, read from the calendar, the weather

66
00:04:22.737 --> 00:04:23.761
and the bookings:

67
00:04:23.761 --> 00:04:28.943
Halloween, a party of twenty four, and Saturday bookings running well ahead of normal.

68
00:04:29.393 --> 00:04:32.798
Then the decisions this week, most urgent first.

69
00:04:32.798 --> 00:04:38.260
Each one says what is wrong, what it costs, and gives you the one button that

70
00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:38.899
fixes it.

71
00:04:38.899 --> 00:04:40.814
Days with no shifts at all.

72
00:04:40.814 --> 00:04:43.864
A day whose labour has run far over target.

73
00:04:43.864 --> 00:04:50.036
People below their contracted hours, who are paid either way, so give them hours first.

74
00:04:50.036 --> 00:04:53.441
And when something is right, it says keep doing.

75
00:04:53.891 --> 00:04:56.046
Below it, the service timeline.

76
00:04:56.046 --> 00:05:02.024
Each day is drawn over its own forecast sales curve, with shifts as bars grouped front

77
00:05:02.024 --> 00:05:07.654
of house, bar and back of house, each showing the person, the role, the hours and

78
00:05:07.654 --> 00:05:08.280
its cost.

79
00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:12.659
The strip beneath reads the hours short or over against demand.

80
00:05:13.109 --> 00:05:18.719
Days with nothing on fold to a single line, with their sales, what is short, and

81
00:05:18.719 --> 00:05:20.683
the decision they belong to.

82
00:05:20.683 --> 00:05:23.909
Open all days, or fold them away, as you like.

83
00:05:24.359 --> 00:05:29.035
And Simple, Standard and Expert set how much the screen shows.

84
00:05:29.035 --> 00:05:34.917
Simple is the decisions and the timeline, for a GM who wants the calm version.

85
00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:37.104
Standard adds the main views.

86
00:05:37.104 --> 00:05:39.744
Expert lays every view out at once.

87
00:05:39.744 --> 00:05:42.911
Each person chooses, and it is remembered.

88
00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.873
Click any shift to open it.

89
00:05:48.873 --> 00:05:53.986
The number that matters is what this shift adds to the week, not a naive rate

90
00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:54.783
times hours.

91
00:05:54.783 --> 00:06:00.627
Aisha is on forty guaranteed hours and has been given eight, so this shift adds nothing:

92
00:06:00.627 --> 00:06:03.150
the business pays that gap either way.

93
00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:06.736
Giving her hours is fairer to her and cheaper for you.

94
00:06:07.186 --> 00:06:09.198
The law is checked as you type.

95
00:06:09.198 --> 00:06:15.427
Cut the unpaid break below the legal minimum and Preshift says what the Working Time Regulations

96
00:06:15.427 --> 00:06:17.698
require for a shift of this length.

97
00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:23.609
Ask for cover puts this shift out to everyone who could legally take it.

98
00:06:23.609 --> 00:06:24.822
For now, cancel.

99
00:06:25.274 --> 00:06:29.691
Now Chloe, a bartender paid by the hour with no guaranteed hours.

100
00:06:29.691 --> 00:06:32.137
Her shift adds its full loaded cost:

101
00:06:32.137 --> 00:06:38.388
gross pay, holiday accrual at twelve point oh seven percent, employer N I at fifteen percent

102
00:06:38.388 --> 00:06:41.650
above the threshold, and auto enrolment pension.

103
00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:46.610
On costs are worked on the whole week, so the rota reconciles to payroll.

104
00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:50.272
You can also work straight on the timeline.

105
00:06:50.272 --> 00:06:55.649
Drag a bar to move it, or drag either end to change the hours in fifteen

106
00:06:55.649 --> 00:06:56.620
minute steps.

107
00:06:56.620 --> 00:07:00.952
Cost, labour percentage and compliance update as you drag.

108
00:07:00.952 --> 00:07:03.716
Here, Sofia finishes an hour earlier.

109
00:07:04.166 --> 00:07:08.347
Drag across empty space on a day to draw a new shift, or click a red,

110
00:07:08.347 --> 00:07:11.922
short hour to fill that gap with the role that is shortest.

111
00:07:11.922 --> 00:07:17.859
The picker ranks who should work it, trained and available, cheapest first, and offers people from

112
00:07:17.859 --> 00:07:22.646
the group's other sites who are set up to cover, with the reason anyone cannot.

113
00:07:26.808 --> 00:07:28.714
The first decision this week:

114
00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:35.025
Wednesday to Sunday have no shifts, with thirty one thousand pounds of forecast sales and nobody

115
00:07:35.025 --> 00:07:35.616
rostered.

116
00:07:35.616 --> 00:07:41.664
Rather than copying last week's rota and hoping, Preshift builds it from the sales forecast.

117
00:07:42.114 --> 00:07:47.762
It turns hourly forecast sales and covers into headcount for each role, fills the gaps peak

118
00:07:47.762 --> 00:07:53.969
first with the cheapest legal person, gives hours to people below their contract before anyone else,

119
00:07:53.969 --> 00:07:55.955
and trims the overstaffed edges.

120
00:07:55.955 --> 00:07:59.058
Press Build the empty days, and watch the numbers.

121
00:07:59.509 --> 00:08:04.809
Built, costed and inside the labour budget, and the decisions update to match.

122
00:08:04.809 --> 00:08:10.517
Gaps that cannot be filled legally with the current team are never hidden or forced.

123
00:08:10.517 --> 00:08:15.613
They are reported as a hiring or cross training signal, not a rota problem.

124
00:08:16.066 --> 00:08:21.391
Scroll down and the whole week is there, every shift on its curve, ready to check

125
00:08:21.391 --> 00:08:22.114
and adjust.

126
00:08:22.564 --> 00:08:25.771
Sign off and publish sits in the line of numbers.

127
00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:31.989
Blocking issues stop publication, so nothing illegal ever reaches the team, and once it is out,

128
00:08:31.989 --> 00:08:35.524
each person hears about their own shifts in good time.

129
00:08:39.696 --> 00:08:45.622
By person shows everyone across the week as a grid, with their hours against contract.

130
00:08:45.622 --> 00:08:48.792
Drag a shift to another person or another day.

131
00:08:49.243 --> 00:08:54.408
The Gantt gives one line per person, shifts as bars against the clock:

132
00:08:54.408 --> 00:08:57.286
the whole week, or one day by the hour.

133
00:08:57.286 --> 00:08:59.795
Drag to move or hand over a shift.

134
00:08:59.795 --> 00:09:04.075
At a site split into areas, it groups and filters by area.

135
00:09:04.526 --> 00:09:06.943
The other six sit behind More views.

136
00:09:06.943 --> 00:09:12.112
Cover map lays the whole week against demand in one grid, so you see where to

137
00:09:12.112 --> 00:09:13.790
add or cut the next hour.

138
00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:19.062
Rest shows last week and this week as one line per person, so a close before

139
00:09:19.062 --> 00:09:23.567
an open, or a long run of days, shows up before it becomes a breach, or

140
00:09:23.567 --> 00:09:24.392
a tired team.

141
00:09:24.843 --> 00:09:27.317
Positions takes one day by position:

142
00:09:27.317 --> 00:09:32.198
who is on the bar, the pass, the door, hour by hour, and where a needed

143
00:09:32.198 --> 00:09:33.435
position is empty.

144
00:09:33.885 --> 00:09:38.834
Shift cost stacks each shift at its loaded cost against the day target.

145
00:09:38.834 --> 00:09:43.365
When labour runs over, this is how you choose which shift to cut.

146
00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:49.456
Changes shows who the next publish will tell, and what, before anyone is told.

147
00:09:51.768 --> 00:09:58.612
And Fairness looks back over four weeks of weekends, closes, late finishes and hours under contract,

148
00:09:58.612 --> 00:10:01.486
to show who keeps getting the hard shifts.

149
00:10:01.486 --> 00:10:04.224
A fair rota is how you keep good people.

150
00:10:04.675 --> 00:10:06.171
Nine views, one week.

151
00:10:06.171 --> 00:10:11.373
Expert lays them all out at once, and the How to guide sets out the order

152
00:10:11.373 --> 00:10:13.867
to use them before a rota goes out.

153
00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:22.093
Ask the assistant lets a GM say what they need in plain English.

154
00:10:22.093 --> 00:10:26.157
Ben is off Saturday, re cover the bar without going over target.

155
00:10:26.157 --> 00:10:32.062
Claude drafts the week by calling the engine's own costing and compliance tools, so it cannot

156
00:10:32.062 --> 00:10:37.014
roster anything illegal, and it leaves shifts that have already started alone.

157
00:10:37.466 --> 00:10:43.204
It works for one site, a company, or the whole group, and nothing changes until you

158
00:10:43.204 --> 00:10:45.071
review and apply the draft.

159
00:10:45.071 --> 00:10:47.768
In this public demo it is switched off.

160
00:10:47.768 --> 00:10:52.538
On your own account it runs live, and an owner can turn it on or off.

161
00:10:52.988 --> 00:11:00.039
Shifty, in the bottom right, answers questions about the rota, labour, the team and holiday from

162
00:11:00.039 --> 00:11:01.434
the app's own data.

163
00:11:01.434 --> 00:11:02.756
Who is on tonight.

164
00:11:02.756 --> 00:11:05.401
What is labour running at this week.

165
00:11:05.401 --> 00:11:07.604
Who has not had a weekend off.

166
00:11:08.054 --> 00:11:14.125
And Tell Preshift, along the bottom, or Control K, takes one line instructions.

167
00:11:14.125 --> 00:11:15.509
Add a new starter.

168
00:11:15.509 --> 00:11:17.891
Ben is ill tonight, find cover.

169
00:11:17.891 --> 00:11:22.502
Each change is shown to you and confirmed before it happens.

170
00:11:26.666 --> 00:11:30.533
Staff ask in the staff app, and the manager decides here.

171
00:11:30.533 --> 00:11:34.942
Holiday, time off, sickness, availability, swaps and open shifts.

172
00:11:34.942 --> 00:11:40.505
Every request is checked again when you approve it, by the same rules as the rota,

173
00:11:40.505 --> 00:11:46.610
so a swap that would break the Working Time Regulations or double book someone is stopped.

174
00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:51.991
Shifts going is one way to put a shift out, whether someone cannot work it or

175
00:11:51.991 --> 00:11:53.015
nobody is on it.

176
00:11:53.015 --> 00:11:59.227
Preshift shows everyone who could legally take it, cheapest first, with what each adds to labour,

177
00:11:59.227 --> 00:12:01.532
and why anyone else is not eligible.

178
00:12:01.984 --> 00:12:03.505
You choose who hears:

179
00:12:03.505 --> 00:12:09.371
everyone eligible now, the cheapest first in rounds, or only the people you tick.

180
00:12:09.371 --> 00:12:10.529
And who decides:

181
00:12:10.529 --> 00:12:14.947
the manager approves a claim, or the first legal yes gets it.

182
00:12:14.947 --> 00:12:18.568
Staff answer in the app, or reply YES on WhatsApp.

183
00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:21.918
Approve claims automatically, site by site.

184
00:12:21.918 --> 00:12:27.107
A claim is approved the moment it is made only when it breaks no rule, raises

185
00:12:27.107 --> 00:12:32.229
nothing to review, and keeps the site's labour that week at or under target.

186
00:12:32.229 --> 00:12:34.116
Anything else waits for you.

187
00:12:38.278 --> 00:12:41.431
The forecast is built from the site's own till.

188
00:12:41.431 --> 00:12:47.267
The same weekday and hour over the last eight weeks, recent weeks counting most, with a

189
00:12:47.267 --> 00:12:48.608
damped trend on top.

190
00:12:48.608 --> 00:12:54.310
Bank holidays trade like past bank holidays, or like a Sunday until there is history.

191
00:12:54.762 --> 00:12:57.665
Then tell the model what it cannot know.

192
00:12:57.665 --> 00:13:00.785
A heatwave, a match down the road, a refit.

193
00:13:00.785 --> 00:13:07.026
Each adjustment is applied as a multiplier, with its reason, when the model next runs.

194
00:13:07.477 --> 00:13:13.369
Demand turns that forecast into headcount for each role, hour by hour, using sales per labour

195
00:13:13.369 --> 00:13:18.691
hour or covers per person, with floors and caps, so a busy night is staffed properly

196
00:13:18.691 --> 00:13:20.845
and a quiet one is not padded out.

197
00:13:21.295 --> 00:13:27.439
Rework from past takings recalibrates those standards from what the site actually traded.

198
00:13:27.889 --> 00:13:30.920
The calendar has the UK trading year built in:

199
00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:36.324
Easter, Mothering Sunday, Halloween, Black Friday, Mad Friday, every bank holiday.

200
00:13:36.324 --> 00:13:42.980
Weather and local events are fetched every morning, bookings come in from the reservation system, and

201
00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:47.593
school holidays by council, so parents on the team can be planned for.

202
00:13:48.044 --> 00:13:50.657
Each item says what to do about it.

203
00:13:50.657 --> 00:13:52.374
A party of twenty four:

204
00:13:52.374 --> 00:13:54.016
roster for it by name.

205
00:13:54.016 --> 00:13:57.301
Saturday dinner pacing well ahead of normal:

206
00:13:57.301 --> 00:14:01.332
build the forecast again and check the rota covers it.

207
00:14:01.332 --> 00:14:03.572
Mark it done, or set it aside.

208
00:14:07.746 --> 00:14:12.889
Coach offers the three changes to this week that save the most without leaving the floor

209
00:14:12.889 --> 00:14:14.350
short or breaking a rule.

210
00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:19.201
Trim an overstaffed edge, take off a shift that is over demand all the way through,

211
00:14:19.201 --> 00:14:22.650
or give a shift to someone cheaper who is trained and free.

212
00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:29.516
Each move shows the saving, loaded with holiday, N I and pension, and the labour percentage

213
00:14:29.516 --> 00:14:30.151
after it.

214
00:14:30.151 --> 00:14:33.324
Take it, and the rota changes there and then.

215
00:14:33.776 --> 00:14:35.137
Below, the ladder.

216
00:14:35.137 --> 00:14:36.650
Four rungs of habit:

217
00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:43.382
the rota on time and legal, labour on target, daypart precision, and owning the forecast.

218
00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:48.677
A site on target with a late rota is lucky, not run, and its team pays

219
00:14:48.677 --> 00:14:49.206
for it.

220
00:14:49.206 --> 00:14:52.232
Coach the habits and the results follow.

221
00:14:56.408 --> 00:15:01.382
Clock in turns a tablet at the staff entrance into a sign in point.

222
00:15:01.382 --> 00:15:06.727
Staff tap an RFID card, or a phone's NFC, or sign in by name, inside the

223
00:15:06.727 --> 00:15:07.914
site's geofence.

224
00:15:07.914 --> 00:15:12.368
It lists who is on today's rota and whether they are in yet.

225
00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.899
Clock in setup holds the rest.

226
00:15:14.899 --> 00:15:20.163
A shared iPad can be paired as a kiosk that does nothing but clock people in

227
00:15:20.163 --> 00:15:20.717
and out.

228
00:15:20.717 --> 00:15:26.259
And in the live product, staff can clock by touching their own phone to a secure

229
00:15:26.259 --> 00:15:27.922
NFC tag at the entrance:

230
00:15:27.922 --> 00:15:31.108
no card, no app to install, iPhone or Android.

231
00:15:31.559 --> 00:15:34.177
Cut call is for the middle of service.

232
00:15:34.177 --> 00:15:39.000
Trading so far from the till is set against forecast to give the pace.

233
00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:44.511
The rest of the day is reforecast at that pace and turned back into headcount by

234
00:15:44.511 --> 00:15:44.855
role.

235
00:15:45.305 --> 00:15:50.186
When trade is behind, it names who to send home early, and the saving is worked

236
00:15:50.186 --> 00:15:55.746
on each person's whole week, after guaranteed hours and the N I and pension thresholds, so

237
00:15:55.746 --> 00:15:58.279
it is what payroll will actually not pay.

238
00:15:58.279 --> 00:16:04.209
And because cuts are tracked, Preshift also watches who keeps being sent home, so nobody quietly

239
00:16:04.209 --> 00:16:05.321
loses their hours.

240
00:16:09.486 --> 00:16:13.591
Payroll runs as five steps, straight through to TeamPay.

241
00:16:13.591 --> 00:16:18.501
In the demo, TeamPay is a simulator, so we can run the whole thing.

242
00:16:18.501 --> 00:16:23.118
First, the people go into TeamPay, one PAYE scheme per company.

243
00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:25.386
Second, clocked hours.

244
00:16:25.386 --> 00:16:29.018
We simulate a week of clocking for the site.

245
00:16:29.477 --> 00:16:35.140
Finished shifts with less rest break than the law gives are flagged before approval, as too

246
00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:39.185
short or split, so nobody is quietly working through their break.

247
00:16:39.185 --> 00:16:44.598
What do I do explains the fix, and the manager approves each person's hours against the

248
00:16:44.598 --> 00:16:44.909
rota.

249
00:16:45.359 --> 00:16:46.477
Third, approve.

250
00:16:46.477 --> 00:16:53.704
Fourth, send the approved hours to TeamPay, one batch per company, through an outbox that retries

251
00:16:53.704 --> 00:16:55.343
and never sends twice.

252
00:16:55.793 --> 00:17:00.792
Fifth, the pay run comes back on a signed webhook and is reconciled to the accrual,

253
00:17:00.792 --> 00:17:05.609
so finance sees the difference between what the rota said and what payroll paid.

254
00:17:09.782 --> 00:17:16.181
Clocked versus rota sets clocked hours against the rota by cause, before they are approved:

255
00:17:16.181 --> 00:17:18.854
late starts, early finishes, overruns.

256
00:17:18.854 --> 00:17:23.846
It fills in as each day closes, with the week's labour flash alongside.

257
00:17:24.296 --> 00:17:30.208
Tronc splits every penny of tips and service charge on clocked hours, so whoever stayed for

258
00:17:30.208 --> 00:17:31.832
the close is paid for it.

259
00:17:31.832 --> 00:17:38.589
Run by an independent troncmaster, the payments carry income tax but no National Insurance, and Preshift

260
00:17:38.589 --> 00:17:43.136
shows the N I saved, the VAT position and the date it must be paid by.

261
00:17:43.586 --> 00:17:47.876
Pay periods runs the close by payroll across a company's sites.

262
00:17:47.876 --> 00:17:53.390
Lock the rota, approve time cards, and pass hours to payroll by the cut off, with

263
00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:56.522
the pay day shown and overdue periods flagged.

264
00:17:56.972 --> 00:17:57.929
Pay approvals.

265
00:17:57.929 --> 00:18:01.347
A change to anyone's rate or salary is a proposal.

266
00:18:01.347 --> 00:18:07.978
Their current pay stays in force until the finance director approves it with their authenticator.

267
00:18:07.978 --> 00:18:14.062
Nobody approves their own proposal or their own pay, and every change shows its full cost

268
00:18:14.062 --> 00:18:14.540
a year.

269
00:18:18.715 --> 00:18:24.491
HR overview puts everything a manager must act on for their people in one list.

270
00:18:24.491 --> 00:18:27.854
Headcount, turnover, absence, and each action:

271
00:18:27.854 --> 00:18:34.728
no return to work conversation, a licence expired, a contract never signed, a fit note missing

272
00:18:34.728 --> 00:18:35.971
after seven days.

273
00:18:36.421 --> 00:18:38.628
Staff holds each employee record:

274
00:18:38.628 --> 00:18:45.449
details, roles, contract and pay, right to work with copies of the documents checked, availability and

275
00:18:45.449 --> 00:18:45.850
leave.

276
00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:51.735
Each record is checked before it reaches the rota, so someone without the right to work,

277
00:18:51.735 --> 00:18:55.213
or paid below the legal minimum, cannot be rostered.

278
00:18:55.664 --> 00:18:58.669
Open a person and their whole file is here:

279
00:18:58.669 --> 00:19:05.240
contract, pay, right to work, training, documents to sign in the staff app, and their history.

280
00:19:05.692 --> 00:19:12.226
Messages keeps one thread per person with their managers, and announcements to a whole site with

281
00:19:12.226 --> 00:19:13.452
who has read them.

282
00:19:13.452 --> 00:19:18.761
Rota notices go out by the app, WhatsApp, text or email, as each person chose.

283
00:19:18.761 --> 00:19:25.228
Everything about work is on record in one place, not scattered across personal WhatsApp groups.

284
00:19:25.678 --> 00:19:32.049
Onboarding gives each new person one checklist, from sixty days before their first day to ninety

285
00:19:32.049 --> 00:19:35.235
days after it, in the order a GM should work it.

286
00:19:35.235 --> 00:19:40.743
The legal steps by day one, payroll and clocking in the first week, training in the

287
00:19:40.743 --> 00:19:41.540
first month.

288
00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:44.062
A good first month is how people stay.

289
00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:53.338
Wellbeing reads the last four weeks and the fortnight ahead for each person.

290
00:19:53.338 --> 00:19:59.040
Long weeks, runs of days, a close then an open, late finishes, no weekend off, missed

291
00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:00.315
breaks, no holiday.

292
00:20:00.315 --> 00:20:05.615
None of these breaks the law, but each one is a conversation to have this week,

293
00:20:05.615 --> 00:20:10.512
with the next step suggested, and a check on how late finishers get home.

294
00:20:10.963 --> 00:20:16.951
Holiday tracks each person's entitlement for their company's leave year, flags anyone who has not had

295
00:20:16.951 --> 00:20:21.931
a break, and shows the holiday pay provision in pounds, ready for the balance sheet.

296
00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:29.235
Absence records sickness and other leave, scores the Bradford factor, and flags every return to work

297
00:20:29.235 --> 00:20:31.017
conversation not yet held.

298
00:20:31.017 --> 00:20:34.788
The cheapest absence control there is, and the kindest.

299
00:20:35.238 --> 00:20:39.326
Training is a matrix of required certificates by role.

300
00:20:39.326 --> 00:20:42.808
Food hygiene, allergens, licensing, first aid.

301
00:20:42.808 --> 00:20:49.924
It shows what an environmental health or licensing visit would find today, and what expires in

302
00:20:49.924 --> 00:20:51.438
the next sixty days.

303
00:20:51.888 --> 00:20:58.801
Probation and reviews tracks probation end dates, so none runs out by default, plus appraisals and

304
00:20:58.801 --> 00:21:01.341
one to ones that are due or overdue.

305
00:21:01.341 --> 00:21:08.184
Cases holds disciplinary and grievance cases, confidential, with the ACAS steps and their timing.

306
00:21:08.635 --> 00:21:14.515
Retention scores who is likely to leave, and why, from what the system already holds:

307
00:21:14.515 --> 00:21:18.804
clocked hours, early finishes, breaks, closes, tenure and pay.

308
00:21:18.804 --> 00:21:23.993
Most of the risk is driven by the rota itself, every point has a reason and

309
00:21:23.993 --> 00:21:28.075
a fix, and the replacement cost at risk is shown in pounds.

310
00:21:28.525 --> 00:21:34.105
Employment rights covers the Employment Rights Act 2025 for zero and low hours workers:

311
00:21:34.105 --> 00:21:39.622
short notice pay owed when a shift is cancelled or cut, and offers of guaranteed hours

312
00:21:39.622 --> 00:21:42.187
that reflect what people regularly work.

313
00:21:42.187 --> 00:21:46.357
The thresholds are settings, ready for when the regulations land.

314
00:21:50.529 --> 00:21:56.994
Labour cost shows every pound payroll will charge, person by person, split into wages, holiday accrual,

315
00:21:56.994 --> 00:22:02.957
employer N I and pension, with rostered hours against contract and a flag wherever the business

316
00:22:02.957 --> 00:22:05.217
is paying for hours it is not using.

317
00:22:05.667 --> 00:22:06.099
Close.

318
00:22:06.099 --> 00:22:11.859
The labour accrual journals, one per company, by role nominal and site tracking.

319
00:22:11.859 --> 00:22:16.899
Post these at week end and the P and L carries true labour on day one.

320
00:22:16.899 --> 00:22:20.211
That is what makes a three day close possible.

321
00:22:20.661 --> 00:22:25.800
Cost lands in the company whose site the work was done at, and the wages accrual

322
00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:30.234
stays with the employer, with the intercompany recharge between them.

323
00:22:30.234 --> 00:22:35.695
Employment Allowance is used against employer N I week by week as payroll applies it.

324
00:22:35.695 --> 00:22:39.357
Download the Xero journal, or post it straight into Xero.

325
00:22:39.807 --> 00:22:40.405
Reports.

326
00:22:40.405 --> 00:22:47.814
GM scorecards ranked on habits before results, the labour trend over four, eight or thirteen weeks,

327
00:22:47.814 --> 00:22:54.999
cost by role and by area, rota against actual, takings, forecast accuracy, and payroll accuracy.

328
00:22:55.449 --> 00:23:00.017
Programme is the twelve week Williams, Stanley labour programme:

329
00:23:00.017 --> 00:23:02.515
Baseline, Control, Optimise, Embed.

330
00:23:02.515 --> 00:23:09.011
Milestones are proved by the site's own data, and the saving is verified against a baseline

331
00:23:09.011 --> 00:23:10.296
from the accounts.

332
00:23:10.296 --> 00:23:14.793
Benchmarks compare your sites with other operators, anonymised.

333
00:23:15.243 --> 00:23:17.688
Prime cost is labour plus cost of sales:

334
00:23:17.688 --> 00:23:22.700
what the two costs a site controls take from every pound sold, with food and drink

335
00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:26.979
margin against what the recipes say, and the leakage in pounds a year.

336
00:23:27.430 --> 00:23:32.392
Compliance risk prices compliance the way a regulator or tribunal would.

337
00:23:32.392 --> 00:23:39.283
Minimum wage arrears owed to staff now, the penalty ceiling, Working Time breaches on clocked hours.

338
00:23:39.283 --> 00:23:44.590
Find the breach first, put it right for the person, and the penalties shrink.

339
00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:51.694
Labour cash shows what each company pays out for its people over the next thirteen weeks,

340
00:23:51.694 --> 00:23:52.367
and when.

341
00:23:52.367 --> 00:23:57.302
Net pay on each pay day, tronc, PAYE and N I to HMRC by the twenty

342
00:23:57.302 --> 00:23:58.873
second, and pensions.

343
00:23:58.873 --> 00:24:04.555
A strong month on the rota is a larger HMRC bill about six weeks later, seen

344
00:24:04.555 --> 00:24:05.752
before it lands.

345
00:24:09.925 --> 00:24:15.964
Set up holds the companies that employ your staff, the sites they trade from, the roles

346
00:24:15.964 --> 00:24:18.602
you roster, and how busy each site is.

347
00:24:18.602 --> 00:24:24.364
Labour cost, the forecast build, compliance and the close journal all run off this.

348
00:24:24.364 --> 00:24:29.639
A site can be split into areas, front of house, back of house, a bakery, and

349
00:24:29.639 --> 00:24:31.861
labour is then reported by area.

350
00:24:32.311 --> 00:24:38.972
Access sets roles for operators, Williams Stanley people and outsiders, scoped by site with start and

351
00:24:38.972 --> 00:24:39.632
end dates.

352
00:24:39.632 --> 00:24:45.963
Nobody grants beyond their own access, paired duties such as setting pay and running payroll are

353
00:24:45.963 --> 00:24:49.327
kept apart, and every change is in the audit trail.

354
00:24:49.777 --> 00:24:53.998
Integrations shows every connection and whether it is working:

355
00:24:53.998 --> 00:24:59.989
the till, TeamPay for each PAYE scheme, Xero, card readers and phone tags, the staff app

356
00:24:59.989 --> 00:25:01.147
and the open API.

357
00:25:01.147 --> 00:25:06.049
Any card not showing connected is a step someone is still doing by hand.

358
00:25:06.499 --> 00:25:12.648
GDPR keeps the request log for access, erasure and the rest, with the one month deadline,

359
00:25:12.648 --> 00:25:20.248
one click subject access export, retention and deletion, and the policy document that holding sickness records

360
00:25:20.248 --> 00:25:20.870
requires.

361
00:25:20.870 --> 00:25:24.187
Staff data is treated with the care it deserves.

362
00:25:24.637 --> 00:25:31.398
Settings connects the till, Claude, email and messaging channels, and makes API keys and webhooks for

363
00:25:31.398 --> 00:25:32.335
other systems.

364
00:25:32.335 --> 00:25:37.824
Features lets an owner switch off the parts of Preshift the business does not use.

365
00:25:37.824 --> 00:25:42.109
Nothing is deleted, and switching back on restores it as it was.

366
00:25:42.559 --> 00:25:45.563
Billing holds the trial and subscription.

367
00:25:45.563 --> 00:25:50.254
Your profile keeps your own details, password and authenticator.

368
00:25:50.254 --> 00:25:57.436
Under Help, How to guides for GMs, and Support, answered by your Williams, Stanley client partner.

369
00:25:57.436 --> 00:26:03.373
And the full REST API is documented, with an MCP connector so Claude can work the

370
00:26:03.373 --> 00:26:04.399
rota directly.

371
00:26:05.352 --> 00:26:08.648
This is the staff app, on each person's own phone.

372
00:26:08.648 --> 00:26:13.987
Today shows whether they are clocked in, their next shift and their recent hours.

373
00:26:13.987 --> 00:26:18.865
They clock in here, by a phone tag at the door or inside the geofence, and

374
00:26:18.865 --> 00:26:20.184
record their breaks.

375
00:26:20.635 --> 00:26:26.176
They can say how their week was, privately, ask for a chat with their manager, and

376
00:26:26.176 --> 00:26:27.798
find someone to talk to.

377
00:26:27.798 --> 00:26:30.907
Their manager only ever sees a site's average.

378
00:26:31.357 --> 00:26:34.732
The Rota tab draws their next two weeks as a strip:

379
00:26:34.732 --> 00:26:37.445
hours, pay before tax, rest and days off.

380
00:26:37.445 --> 00:26:41.019
Ben has nothing published yet for the fortnight ahead.

381
00:26:41.019 --> 00:26:46.446
Once the week goes out, each shift appears here beside the people on with him, and

382
00:26:46.446 --> 00:26:51.013
he can offer it to a named colleague, swap, or pick up an open shift.

383
00:26:51.464 --> 00:26:58.152
Requests is where they ask for holiday against their balance, time off, report sickness, and set

384
00:26:58.152 --> 00:26:59.475
when they can work.

385
00:26:59.475 --> 00:27:01.496
A real say in their own rota.

386
00:27:01.947 --> 00:27:04.843
Pay shows their payslips and their tips.

387
00:27:04.843 --> 00:27:10.563
Inbox holds every message from their managers, announcements, and rota notices.

388
00:27:11.518 --> 00:27:12.668
That is Preshift.

389
00:27:12.668 --> 00:27:17.880
A rota sized to the forecast, fair to the people who work it, legal before it

390
00:27:17.880 --> 00:27:23.769
is published, and costed the way payroll will cost it, in the ledger before payroll has

391
00:27:23.769 --> 00:27:24.039
run.

392
00:27:24.039 --> 00:27:26.950
Look after your team, and the numbers hold.
